60
00:06:49.148 --> 00:07:02.505
<v Daniel>Well, I mean, it's one thing to look at stats and predict who scores, like the Ashok Kumar paper did, but it's entirely different to draw up the playbook explaining why the defense left the receiver open in the first place. That's theory building.</v>

61
00:07:02.894 --> 00:07:04.115
<v Maya>That is a great way to look at it.</v>

62
00:07:04.536 --> 00:07:17.307
<v Daniel>And my initial assumption going into this was that predicting human behavior in social science is fundamentally too messy for an AI. Like, surely it requires some lived human context, right?</v>

